       "type": "text",
       "text": "I haven't entered this order. 1700 mg three times daily comes to 5,100 mg/day, which is about twice the maximum labeled metformin dose. The maximum is 2,550 mg/day for immediate-release, given as up to 850 mg three times daily. A dose this high raises the risk of lactic acidosis and GI toxicity, even with normal renal function.\n\nCould this be a typo? Some possible intended orders:\n- **850 mg PO three times daily with meals** (2,550 mg/day, the maximum for immediate-release)\n- **500 mg PO three times daily with meals** (1,500 mg/day)\n- **1,700 mg/day total**, for example 850 mg PO twice daily with meals\n\nIf 1,700 mg three times daily is what you want, tell me and add a note on the clinical rationale. I can then enter it with that note. Otherwise, tell me the corrected dose and I'll enter it right away."
